<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herod Archelaus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">23 BCE – c. 18 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herod Archelaus was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> who ruled Judea, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idumaea">Idumaea</a> as ethnarch from 4 BCE to 6 CE, after Augustus denied him the royal title. His harsh rule provoked complaints from both Judeans and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaritans">Samaritans</a>, and Augustus deposed him and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Judea then came under the direct rule of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prefect">prefects</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herod-archelaus.jpg" alt="Herod Archelaus" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archelaus_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
